 {"question" "q-80503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{x}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles I and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle II covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/state.json" "file_sha256" "445f5e89ba92e63db22e187ad5e36c375e0f63a01971bda887285e96077926af" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80503" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1dd6b5880f7162c5e89d5d9a910fa55ae62fc84f22fc6ebcef9e0368d226dae3" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80503" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/state.json" "file_sha256" "445f5e89ba92e63db22e187ad5e36c375e0f63a01971bda887285e96077926af" "basis" 1791 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053940/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8050